From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:38:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] backends: let cursor implementations decline a cursor

The cursor theme always built its cursors with the highest priority
implementation. A shell that draws scalable cursors then replaced every
Xcursor theme with its own fallback. Implementations that are initable
can now fail to initialize, and the next one in priority order is tried,
so Xcursor themes keep working next to scalable ones.
---
 src/backends/meta-cursor-theme.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/meta-cursor-theme.c b/src/backends/meta-cursor-theme.c
index 36431184d3a50d1e56d00f22d4138cead15c37ee..60763d8de34b71f58818f5e0446927853c6def7c 100644
--- a/src/backends/meta-cursor-theme.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-cursor-theme.c
@@ -155,7 +155,13 @@ meta_cursor_theme_get_cursor (MetaCursorTheme   *cursor_theme,
                                  "size", meta_prefs_get_cursor_size (),
                                  NULL);
 
-          g_assert (cursor != NULL);
+          if (G_IS_INITABLE (cursor) &&
+              !g_initable_init (G_INITABLE (cursor), NULL, NULL))
+            {
+              g_clear_object (&cursor);
+              continue;
+            }
+
           break;
         }
 
